{
  "name": "envmap-sample",
  "description": "An experimental build system and sample project designed to compile Java applications into Actually Portable Executables (APE) by integrating GraalVM Native Image with Cosmopolitan Libc. It automates the orchestration of patching GraalVM, bootstrapping a LabsJDK-based toolchain, and leveraging cosmocc for cross-architecture static linking. The resulting binaries are platform-agnostic, single-file executables capable of running across various operating systems and architectures without an external runtime environment.",
